                <pb facs="0507" n="498" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg498"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.51/4613: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hinkle</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ciudad
                                Trujillo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-06-10T09:00:00-05:00">June 10, 1938—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>33. The President on being informed of contents of Department’s telegram No. 22,
                    June 8, 3 p.m., indicated that he would have a proposal made as soon as
                    possible. He suggested that the Foreign Secretary in drawing up his proposal
                    should consult with Minister Norweb whenever possible.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hinkle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
